    "content": "All 22 checklist items are tested and recorded — **18 PASS, 4 FAIL**.\n\n## Failures\n\n| ID | Issue |\n|---|---|\n| **FT-19** | **No persistence.** Product data lives only in in-memory React state (localStorage/sessionStorage/cookies all empty). Reloading wiped the created product and reverted every edit to seed values. This also bit mid-session: pressing Enter in the header search box submits a real `<form>`, causing a full navigation that silently destroyed unsaved catalog work. |\n| **CS-20** | **No publish validation.** Only Name, Category and Short Description are required. A product saved successfully with price `-50` (rendered `-$50`), no image, no retailer link, no full review and zero specifications. The price input lacks a `min` attribute. Rating was the one correctly bounded field (`min=0/max=5`). |\n| **FT-2** | **Featured set not fully browsable.** \"Editor's Top Picks\" is hard-capped at 3, so marking a 4th product featured produced no visible homepage change. Its \"View all\" link targets `/products?featured=true`, but that page ignores the param — it showed all 9 products including non-featured ones — and there is no featured filter control anywhere. |\n| **FT-4** | **Tag-filter list is static.** New tags save, display on the detail page and are keyword-searchable, but the Filters → Tags list only ever offers the 35 seed-derived tags, so a newly assigned tag can never be selected as a filter. |\n\n## Notable\nAn early run of FT-3/FT-5/FT-9 appeared to fail, but the cause was the FT-19 reload bug wiping state mid-test. I re-created the data and re-ran those items via client-side navigation only; all three genuinely pass. Also worth flagging: the price \"range\" control is a single max-price slider whose thumb is labelled *Minimum* and ignores keyboard input (drag-only), and seeded retailer links point to `example.com` placeholders.\n\nSearch, sorting, multi-criteria filtering, category assignment, detail-page content, cross-view consistency and not-found handling all behave correctly."
  }
}
